// float() reads a text as a number with the same rule as the comparisons: a
// number written with an optional sign, decimals and exponent, spaces around
// allowed. Any other text, and any value that is not a number, a text or a
// boolean, gives 0. The same on every target.

state
  list: [1]

function inFunction(value)
  return float(value)

beat Start
  Numbers give ${float("3.14")} ${float(" 5 ")} ${float("-2")} ${float(".5")} ${float("1e3")} ${float("2.5e-1")}.

  Not numbers give ${float("5abc")} ${float("abc")} ${float("")} ${float(" ")} ${float("0x10")} ${float("Infinity")} ${float("1,5")}.

  Other values give ${float(true)} ${float(false)} ${float(null)} ${float(7)} ${float(list)}.

  In a function gives ${inFunction("3.14")} ${inFunction("5abc")} ${inFunction(true)}.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ Numbers give 3.14 5 -2 0.5 1000 0.25.

    ~ Not numbers give 0 0 0 0 0 0 0.

    ~ Other values give 1 0 0 7 0.

    ~ In a function gives 3.14 0 1.
</test>
*/
